  "claim_boundary": "For a finite-horizon feature MDP, an exogenously selected consequence level preserves the original occupancy query when the state/action sets, initial distribution, transition kernel, horizon, and target feature map are unchanged. A complete scalar value rectangle supplies the declared additive consequence exactly when every anchored increment equals the declared offset increment; this imposes m(n-1) independent constraints and every constraint is necessary. Mechanical data alone cannot certify the semantic coefficient, and an unknown coefficient remains scale-coupled under a rescalable response-link class. If every anchored calibration residual is at most epsilon, every two-sided offset bias is at most 2 epsilon, sharply. These are classical exogenous-decomposition, additive-measurement, reward-invariance, and finite-linear-algebra ingredients; no novelty is claimed. The result does not establish that any real consequence has stable cardinal utility, infer scalar values from ordinal data, validate a demonstrator model, or resolve ASMP-9.",
